  "summary": "ACCEPT. The exact pinned boundary and all artifact hashes were verified. The final candidate resolves every prior blocking finding: it rejects dirty reusable checkouts and binds CodeGraph profiling, framework/profile readers, and communication detection to one safely materialized private committed Git tree; it fails closed for tracked-byte mutation without a HEAD change, snapshot mutation, revision advancement, and downstream Profiled Revision mismatch. The detector interface and profile-only-to-composite lifecycle are non-circular, and the Core-owned immutable handoff read model preserves the Core-to-Infrastructure-to-Web-to-Shared dependency direction. Confirmed-kind flags and pre-truncation counts remain authoritative, the fingerprint binds the Profiled Revision and complete normalized evidence, and deterministic reservation preserves one direct sample for each confirmed kind in the more-than-100 both-kind case. Confirmed evidence is projected through the Core read model, Shared DTO, authorized Web mapping, bounded redaction contract, and integration tests. Story 4.3 retains DbContext, model-snapshot, and migration ownership through its completed-story checkpoint, and Story 11.1 must base migration work on that exact published SHA. Canonical glossary terms, RPC/HTTP-only deadline scope, explicit exclusions, ManagementAccess and Repository visibility, transient RED-GREEN TDD, security/redaction checks, migration verification, combined review, and current-boundary integration coverage all align with the Constitution, current authorities, and expedited-MVP exception. No unresolved ADR conflict or blocking feasibility, architecture, failure-behavior, compliance, or testability issue remains. This accepted plan still triggers the mandatory planned-change authorization before task generation."
